---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import { LINKEDIN_URL, SCHEDULING_LINK } from '../consts';

const influences = [
	{
		name: 'Shape Up',
		href: 'https://basecamp.com/shapeup',
		note: 'from Basecamp. Fixed time, variable scope. It’s why the budget is fixed and the scope moves.',
	},
	{
		name: 'The Lean Startup',
		href: 'https://theleanstartup.com/',
		note: 'by Eric Ries. The experiment as the unit of work.',
	},
	{
		name: 'Incorruptible',
		href: 'https://www.simonandschuster.com/books/Incorruptible/Eric-Ries/9798893311860',
		note: 'Eric Ries again. Build things that create more value than they take.',
	},
	{
		name: 'Design thinking',
		href: 'https://designthinking.ideo.com/',
		note: 'as IDEO teaches it. Put the thing in real hands before you trust your own opinion of it.',
	},
	{
		name: 'Pivotal Labs',
		href: 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pivotal_Labs',
		note: 'where a team learns all of this by doing it next to someone for a few months.',
	},
];

// The month chart: one experiment in month 1, two in month 2, four in month 3.
// Each arc is one experiment; its height grows with its length.
const base = 150;
const months = [
	{ from: 40, to: 347, n: 1 },
	{ from: 347, to: 653, n: 2 },
	{ from: 653, to: 960, n: 4 },
];
const arcs = months.flatMap((m) => {
	const len = (m.to - m.from) / m.n;
	return Array.from({ length: m.n }, (_, i) => {
		const a = m.from + i * len;
		const b = a + len;
		return { d: `M ${a} ${base} Q ${(a + b) / 2} ${base - 0.6 * len} ${b} ${base}`, end: b };
	});
});
---

<MarketingLayout
	title="Work | People Purpose Product"
	description="Fractional product lead and product coaching for nonprofits and impact-focused organizations, and what a typical month looks like."
>
	<section class="wrap">
		<div class="measure page-header">
			<h1>Work</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Your product owner knows the community and makes the final call. A product lead brings
				those ideas to life and tests them quickly, so you know what's worth scaling for your
				users.
			</p>
			<p class="lede">
				That's the job I do for you. When you want it, it's also the job I teach someone on
				your team, so it keeps going after I'm gone.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap ways">
		<div class="label ruled">How we work together</div>
		<div class="venn-row">
			<figure class="venn">
				<svg viewBox="90 0 500 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="venn-t">
					<title id="venn-t">Two circles: I do it, and I teach it. The overlap, both, is where we start.</title>
					<defs>
						<clipPath id="venn-left"><circle cx="255" cy="165" r="150"></circle></clipPath>
					</defs>
					<circle cx="425" cy="165" r="150" class="v-tint" clip-path="url(#venn-left)"></circle>
					<circle cx="255" cy="165" r="150" class="v-ring"></circle>
					<circle cx="425" cy="165" r="150" class="v-ring"></circle>
					<text x="190" y="165" class="v-k" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="middle">I do it</text>
					<text x="340" y="165" class="v-k v-mid" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="middle">Both</text>
					<text x="490" y="165" class="v-k" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="middle">I teach it</text>
				</svg>
			</figure>
			<div class="way-notes">
				<div class="on">
					<h3>Both <span class="pill">Where we start</span></h3>
					<p class="sub">Doing and coaching</p>
					<p>We do the work together, and someone on your team takes it over. Someone has to keep the product going after I leave.</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h3>I do it</h3>
					<p class="sub">Fractional product lead</p>
					<p>I run the tests and bring you a recommendation. Fits when nobody has hours for the product work yet.</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h3>I teach it</h3>
					<p class="sub">Product coaching</p>
					<p>You do the work, and I coach you through it. Fits when someone has the instincts and needs the craft.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap">
		<div class="month">
			<h2>What the first months look like</h2>
			<p class="measure">
				At a minimum, one real experiment reaches your users each month. Ultimately, we move as
				fast as your team can. The first experiment takes the longest to gather results, and we
				will aim to make every subsequent experiment move faster.
			</p>
			<figure class="track">
				<svg viewBox="0 44 1000 150" role="img" aria-labelledby="track-t">
					<title id="track-t">Three months. One experiment reaches users in the first month, two in the second, and four in the third.</title>
					{arcs.map((a) => <path d={a.d} class="t-arc"></path>)}
					<line x1="40" y1="150" x2="960" y2="150" class="t-base"></line>
					<line x1="347" y1="140" x2="347" y2="160" class="t-tick"></line>
					<line x1="653" y1="140" x2="653" y2="160" class="t-tick"></line>
					<circle cx="40" cy="150" r="6" class="t-start"></circle>
					{arcs.map((a) => <circle cx={a.end} cy="150" r="6" class="t-hands"></circle>)}
					<text x="193" y="182" class="t-month" text-anchor="middle">Month 1</text>
					<text x="500" y="182" class="t-month" text-anchor="middle">Month 2</text>
					<text x="807" y="182" class="t-month" text-anchor="middle">Month 3</text>
				</svg>
			</figure>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap">
		<div class="measure influences">
			<h2>Where this comes from</h2>
			<p>My school of product ownership had many teachers. A few I keep going back to:</p>
			<ul>
				{influences.map((i) => (
					<li><a href={i.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{i.name}</a>, {i.note}</li>
				))}
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap">
		<div class="measure closing">
			<h2>Let's talk</h2>
			<p>
				If any of this resonates, I'd love to talk. Book 30 minutes and tell me what
				you're working on.
			</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="primary" href={SCHEDULING_LINK} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Find a time &rarr;</a>
				<span class="aside">Prefer email? Write me at <a class="email-link" href={LINKEDIN_URL}>hello at this domain</a>.</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</MarketingLayout>

<script>
	// Assemble the address in the browser so scrapers reading the raw HTML
	// never see a complete email. The href above is a fallback (LinkedIn)
	// for the rare no-JS visitor.
	const user = 'hello';
	const domain = 'peoplepurposeproduct.com';
	const address = `${user}@${domain}`;
	document.querySelectorAll('.email-link').forEach((el) => {
		el.setAttribute('href', `mailto:${address}`);
		el.textContent = address;
	});
</script>

<style>
	.page-header {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 24px;
		padding: 96px 0 56px;
	}
	.lede {
		font-size: 22px;
		line-height: 1.45;
		color: var(--body);
	}

	/* How we work together: the Venn beside one note per region. */
	.ways {
		--tint: rgba(63, 107, 79, 0.1);
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 32px;
		padding-bottom: 56px;
	}
	.venn-row {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: 56px;
		align-items: center;
	}
	.venn {
		margin: 0;
	}
	svg {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		font-family: "Newsreader", Georgia, serif;
	}
	.v-ring {
		fill: none;
		stroke: var(--text);
		stroke-width: 1;
	}
	.v-tint {
		fill: var(--tint);
	}
	.v-k {
		font-size: 24px;
		fill: var(--text);
	}
	.v-mid {
		fill: var(--link);
	}
	.way-notes {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
	}
	.way-notes > div {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 4px;
		padding: 18px 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}
	.way-notes > div.on {
		border-top-color: var(--link);
	}
	.way-notes h3 {
		font-size: 22px;
	}
	.way-notes .on h3 {
		color: var(--link);
	}
	.way-notes .sub {
		font-size: 16px;
		font-style: italic;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	.way-notes p:last-child {
		font-size: 17px;
		line-height: 1.5;
	}
	.pill {
		margin-left: 10px;
		font-size: 11px;
		line-height: 1;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--link);
		border: 1px solid var(--link);
		border-radius: 999px;
		padding: 4px 8px 3px;
		vertical-align: 3px;
		white-space: nowrap;
	}

	/* The month chart: each arc is one experiment, the axis is time. */
	.track {
		margin: 8px 0 0;
	}
	.t-base {
		stroke: var(--text);
		stroke-width: 1.5;
	}
	.t-tick {
		stroke: var(--text);
		stroke-width: 1;
	}
	.t-arc {
		fill: none;
		stroke: var(--link);
		stroke-width: 2.5;
	}
	.t-start {
		fill: var(--bg);
		stroke: var(--text);
		stroke-width: 1.5;
	}
	.t-hands {
		fill: var(--link);
	}
	.t-month {
		font-size: 15px;
		fill: var(--muted);
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.month,
	.influences {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 18px;
		padding: 32px 0 56px;
	}
	.month p,
	.influences p,
	.closing p {
		font-size: 19px;
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: var(--body);
	}
	.month {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
		padding-top: 48px;
	}
	.influences ul {
		padding-left: 1.2em;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 8px;
		font-size: 19px;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--body);
	}
	.influences {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
		padding-top: 48px;
	}

	.closing {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 18px;
		padding: 48px 0 72px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.page-header {
			padding: 48px 0 40px;
			gap: 18px;
		}
		.lede {
			font-size: 20px;
		}
		.venn-row {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 24px;
		}
		.venn {
			max-width: 320px;
			justify-self: center;
		}
		.month,
		.influences {
			padding: 24px 0 48px;
		}
		.closing {
			padding: 40px 0 56px;
		}
	}
</style>
